From 920ec37de73e3aa606faae8baca9a85335008d82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paperclip Agent <agent@paperclip.local>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 04:35:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(meta): stamp per-conversation prompt_cache_key on Muse
 Responses requests

Derive a stable per-conversation prompt_cache_key for Meta Responses
requests so Meta routes each conversation to backends that already hold
its prefix. Precedence: an explicit client key (payload, original
request, or translated body) is preserved; otherwise the key is a
UUIDv5 over the conversation session identity (execution session first,
then derived identity, then request-context session), namespaced by
upstream model. With no session identity no key is set: a
credential-scoped fallback would pin every conversation on one
credential to the same backends.

prompt_cache_retention stays stripped: it is a server-side eviction
hint, orthogonal to the routing key.
---
 .../runtime/executor/meta_executor_execute.go |   7 +
 .../runtime/executor/meta_prompt_cache_key.go |  54 ++++
 .../executor/meta_prompt_cache_key_test.go    | 290 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 351 insertions(+)
